---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Grossline — monthly reporting for Shopify DTC brands"
  description="The ad platforms and your store rarely agree. Grossline shows both numbers and reports on what your store actually made — blended across Shopify, Google and Meta."
  path="/"
  wide
>
  <h1>The ad platforms and your store rarely agree.</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Grossline shows you both numbers, side by side, and reports on what your store actually made —
    blended across Shopify, Google and Meta.
  </p>

  <div class="claimgap">
    <div class="cell">
      <div class="k">Meta reports</div>
      <div class="v">195</div>
      <div class="k">conversions, August</div>
    </div>
    <div class="cell store">
      <div class="k">Your store recorded</div>
      <div class="v">124</div>
      <div class="k">orders, August</div>
    </div>
    <div class="note">
      A 36% claim gap. We show it plainly and decide on store-recorded orders — never a platform's
      own count.
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="demo-note">
    Figures from a demo tenant with realistic seeded data — not a real merchant's numbers.
  </p>

  <h2>What you get</h2>
  <div class="cols">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>One blended picture</h3>
      <p>
        Shopify orders with Google and Meta spend in the same view — revenue and advertising cost,
        finally together. No attribution guesswork.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Findings worth acting on</h3>
      <p>
        A short, ranked set each month: where money is leaking, and where there is room to grow —
        each framed as a bounded test, never a guess.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>An analyst behind it</h3>
      <p>
        Consistent definitions, currency-aware numbers, reconciled against the platforms. A report
        someone stands behind.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Pricing you can predict</h2>
  <p>
    <span class="flat">Flat monthly fee, based on your ad spend</span>
    &nbsp;— never a percentage of revenue. That is the direct contrast with every other tool, and
    the thing their current one annoys them about.
  </p>
  <p><a href="/pricing">See the three plans →</a></p>

  <h2>See a real report</h2>
  <p class="lede">
    The clearest way to understand the product is to read one. Request your free first report — it
    is the service delivered once, at no charge, not a demo of software.
  </p>
  <p>
    <a class="btn" href="/free-report">Request your free first report</a>
    &nbsp; <a href="/the-report">or see what's in it</a>
  </p>
</Base>
